[list]
[*]Fixed: a colonist in uniform who flew off on a gravship while their outfit stand stayed behind, on a map without a grav anchor, kept the uniform force-worn for good, so their apparel policy never replaced it. The takeoff abandons that map, and the stand and the clothes parked in it go with it, as before. The uniform now becomes ordinary clothing as the ship leaves. The same holds for a stand left on any other map that is abandoned while its colonist is away.
[*]A colonist already stuck this way keeps the forced flag after the update: press Clr. forced for them once, on the Assign tab.
[*]Unchanged: a gravship that carries a colonist and their stand together changes nothing, and they change back after landing as usual. A flight that parts them while the map left behind is kept by a grav anchor leaves the colonist in uniform until the two are on one map again, and from then on they change back as usual.
[/list]
